      "content": "I hear you on the institutional side, but when you look at the actual data from these regions, it often feels like those \"strong institutions\" are just a theory. In practice, we see so much more volatility in multi-ethnic African or SE Asian states compared to, say, much more monolithic Western or East Asian nations. Is it fair to say that the inherent complexity of managing competing ethnic identities in these specific types of developing regions creates a fundamentally different risk profile that we just can't ignore?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
